  "description": "Fuselage: Black all over. Cheatlines: None; from just ahead of the wing to ahead of the tail, the profiles of 14 young people (children, grandchildren and mentees of Alaska employees) in copper, amber and brown silhouettes, from the crown down to the belly behind the wing. Tail: Black with 'Alaska' in dark gray reading up the fin. Engines: Black with the UNCF logo. Winglets: Black. Titles: A quote on each side ahead of the profiles, in condensed capitals in orange and off-white: on the left Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.'s 'The time is always right to do what is right.', on the right Nelson Mandela's 'Education is the most powerful weapon we can use to change the world.' Typography by Adé Hogue. Colors hex: not published; matched by eye.",
